{"orgCode":"7870","name":"California Victim Compensation Board","agencyCode":"7500","agencyName":"Government Operations","description":"The governing body of the California Victim Compensation Board (CalVCB) consists of three members: the Secretary of the Government Operations Agency who serves as the chair, the State Controller, and a public member appointed by the Governor. CalVCB provides responsive financial compensation to remedy the financial burdens of victims of crime through the Restitution Fund. The primary objectives of CalVCB are to:\n\n• Compensate victims of violent crime and eligible family members for certain crime-related financial losses.\n\n• Determine the eligibility of individuals for compensation for injury sustained through erroneous conviction and imprisonment.\n\n• Process claims for the Missing Children Reward Program to assist local law enforcement agencies or other parties involved in the identification and recovery of missing children in California.\n\n• Process claims through the Good Samaritan Program to private citizens who are injured rescuing another person, preventing a crime, or assisting a law enforcement officer.","website":"https://www.vcgcb.ca.gov","totals":{"amounts":{"py":131191,"cy":170779,"by":179786},"positions":{"py":246.7,"cy":284,"by":284}},"programs":{"id":"exp/7500/7870","kind":"department","name":"California Victim Compensation Board","code":"7870","amounts":{"py":131191,"cy":170779,"by":179786},"positions":{"py":246.7,"cy":284,"by":284},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":28098,"cy":42035,"by":61328},"special":{"py":72540,"cy":92730,"by":82450},"federal":{"py":30553,"cy":36014,"by":36008}},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7870/6380","kind":"program","name":"Victim Compensation","code":"6380","amounts":{"py":119565,"cy":155276,"by":164276},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":28098,"cy":42035,"by":61328},"special":{"py":60914,"cy":77227,"by":66940},"federal":{"py":30553,"cy":36014,"by":36008}},"positions":{"py":159.9,"cy":188,"by":188},"description":"6380 - VICTIM COMPENSATION PROGRAM\n\nThis program reimburses certain expenses of victims of crime in California who are injured or threatened with injury and suffer financial hardship as a direct result of a violent crime. The victim of a qualifying crime, and eligible family members, may file a claim with the CalVCB for program benefits.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":34896,"cy":42558,"by":42537},"Local Assistance":{"py":84669,"cy":112718,"by":121739}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7870/6380/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":28098,"cy":42035,"by":61328},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":28098,"cy":42035,"by":61328}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":897,"cy":1300,"by":1328},"Local Assistance":{"py":27201,"cy":40735,"by":60000}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7870/6380/f0214","kind":"fund","name":"Restitution Fund","code":"0214","amounts":{"py":50841,"cy":68115,"by":58072},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":50841,"cy":68115,"by":58072}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":32768,"cy":39440,"by":39397},"Local Assistance":{"py":18073,"cy":28675,"by":18675}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7870/6380/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":30553,"cy":36014,"by":36008},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":30553,"cy":36014,"by":36008}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":581,"cy":1818,"by":1812},"Local Assistance":{"py":29972,"cy":34196,"by":34196}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7870/6380/f3383","kind":"fund","name":"Forced or Involuntary Sterilization Compensation Account","code":"3383","amounts":{"py":650,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":650,"cy":0,"by":0}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":650,"cy":0,"by":0}}}},{"id":"exp/7500/7870/6380/f3286","kind":"fund","name":"Safe Neighborhoods and Schools Fund","code":"3286","amounts":{"py":9423,"cy":9112,"by":8868},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":9423,"cy":9112,"by":8868}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":9423,"cy":9112,"by":8868}}}}]},{"id":"exp/7500/7870/6385","kind":"program","name":"Restitution Program","code":"6385","amounts":{"py":11626,"cy":15483,"by":15490},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":11626,"cy":15483,"by":15490}},"positions":{"py":22.8,"cy":25,"by":25},"description":"6385 - RESTITUTION PROGRAM\n\nThis program serves victims of crime in California by maintaining the fiscal stability of the Restitution Fund through the recovery of monies owed from restitution fines and orders. The Program's chief emphasis is to educate the criminal justice community (the judiciary, district attorneys, chief probation officers, and court administrators) on the importance of the consistent imposition and collection of restitution fines and orders. The program also partners with the Department of Corrections and Rehabilitation, the Franchise Tax Board, and the Attorney General's Office on restitution-related activities.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":6959,"cy":8166,"by":8173},"Local Assistance":{"py":4667,"cy":7317,"by":7317}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/7500/7870/6385/f0214","kind":"fund","name":"Restitution Fund","code":"0214","amounts":{"py":11626,"cy":15483,"by":15490},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":11626,"cy":15483,"by":15490}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":6959,"cy":8166,"by":8173},"Local Assistance":{"py":4667,"cy":7317,"by":7317}}}}]},{"id":"exp/7500/7870/6395","kind":"program","name":"Good Samaritan","code":"6395","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"6395 - GOOD SAMARITAN PROGRAM\n\nThis program reimburses persons who sustained injury for certain expenses or losses as a result of a direct actio